From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: dcomp: Windows.UI.Composition, a first slice drawn with Direct2D

Windows.UI.Composition.Compositor and CompositorController are activatable
from dcomp.dll. The first slice has:
 - container and sprite visuals, with offset, size, opacity, visibility
   and an inset clip; a visual collection;
 - color brushes and surface brushes;
 - a graphics device made from a Direct2D or DXGI device, and drawing
   surfaces (ICompositionDrawingSurfaceInterop: BeginDraw hands out the
   device context already drawing, or a DXGI surface or texture; EndDraw,
   Resize, Scroll);
 - surfaces for composition swap chains (ICompositorInterop);
 - desktop window targets (ICompositorDesktopInterop).

Changes are committed from the thread's message loop. With a
CompositorController the loop raises CommitNeeded; without one it commits
directly. A target is rendered into an offscreen bitmap with the program's
own Direct2D device, read back and drawn into the window with GDI. Swap
chain surfaces are placed over it through the composition swap chains of
0190.

New IDL: windows.ui.composition.core.idl (CompositorController),
windows.ui.composition.desktop.idl (DesktopWindowTarget), and the interop
interfaces. The IIDs are the public ones.

Gate: test/wuicomp-gate.sh.
