+/*
+ * A first slice of the visual layer. A compositor owns a tree of visuals
+ * per desktop window target; container visuals hold children, sprite
+ * visuals paint their size with a brush (a colour, or a surface: a drawing
+ * surface a program draws into with Direct2D through
+ * ICompositionDrawingSurfaceInterop). Committing -- the compositor
+ * controller's Commit, or, without one, soon after a change -- draws each
+ * target's tree into a swap chain on its window, with Direct2D on the
+ * device the program gave the compositor (ICompositorInterop), so its
+ * surfaces are drawn without copies. There is no desktop compositor here to
+ * put the tree above or below the window's own drawing: the tree covers the
+ * window. Animations, effects brushes and property sets are not there yet.
+ */
